<Base title="Privacy" description="What Mission Bay News collects from residents, why, and who can see it.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Mission Bay News is run by resident volunteers. We keep what we collect to a minimum.</p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>We do not run accounts or tracking on this website, and your text-size choice is saved only in your own browser. The only outside services are Google Translate (only if you choose Chinese, see below) and ads from Google, if the site shows them (see Advertising and cookies below).</p>
  <p>If you choose <strong>繁體中文</strong> or <strong>简体中文</strong> at the top of a page, your browser loads Google Translate to translate the page, and Google may collect data under its own privacy policy. That happens only after you click one of those buttons. Choose <strong>English</strong> to switch it off. The translation is automatic and may contain mistakes.</p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>Mission Bay News may show ads served by Google AdSense. If it does:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google and other third-party vendors use cookies to show ads based on a visitor's earlier visits to this website or other websites.</li>
    <li>Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and its partners show ads to you based on your visit to this site and other sites on the internet.</li>
    <li>You can turn off personalized ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some other companies' personalized ads at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
    <li>We do not give advertisers your name or contact details, and we never use sign-up form answers for advertising.</li>
    <li>Ads are paid placements, not endorsements by Mission Bay News or the residents' association. We cannot check every advertiser.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Learn how Google uses data from sites that use its services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p>

  <h2>What the sign-up form collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, space number and email address.</li>
    <li>Your phone number, only if you choose to give it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The form is on a separate service (Google Forms). Answers go to a private spreadsheet that only a small number of named volunteers can open.</p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>Only to confirm that you live in Mission Bay and to give you access to the residents' area. We do not sell or share it, and we do not give it to park management or anyone else.</p>

  <h2>The survey</h2>
  <p>The resident survey is anonymous. It does not ask for your name, and we cannot link answers to a person.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Sign-up answers are deleted once you are approved or declined, and the approved-member list is checked every year. People who move away are removed.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see, correct or remove your details, or leave the group, at any time. <a href="/contact/">Contact the editor</a>.</p>

  <h2>Group rules</h2>
  <p>Residents' group posts are for residents only. Please do not share what others post outside the group.</p>
</Base>
